{% set stereo = evidence.stereo_context %}
{% set has_downmix = stereo.schema == 'chipmunk.stereo-channel-context/2' %}
<div class="multimedia-acoustic-summary" id="multimedia-stereo-context">
<h3>{% if evidence.kind == 'video' %}Stereo soundtrack comparison{% else %}Stereo channel comparison{% endif %}</h3>
{% if stereo.status == 'mono' %}<p>The first audio stream is mono. Channel comparison does not apply.</p>
{% elif stereo.status == 'unsupported' %}<p>The first audio stream does not have a supported two-channel layout.</p>
{% elif stereo.status == 'too_short' %}<p>The stereo input has less than one complete second of decoded audio.</p>
{% elif stereo.status == 'unavailable' %}<p>The stereo measurements could not be aligned to the recorded source clock.</p>
{% else %}
<p>Compared {{ stereo.windows | length }} complete one-second windows in the first {{ stereo.max_seconds }} seconds {% if has_downmix %}using the decoded stereo channels and the analyzed mono mix{% else %}before mono mixing{% endif %}. Stereo placement, mixing and microphone position can all affect these readings. They do not contribute to the AI assessment.</p>
{% if stereo.status == 'quiet' %}<p>All measured windows fell below the {{ stereo.quiet_floor_dbfs }} dBFS review floor.</p>{% endif %}
{% if has_downmix %}
{% set attenuated = stereo.windows | selectattr('downmix.strong_attenuation') | list %}
{% if attenuated %}<p><strong>Strong level drop in the analyzed mono mix.</strong> {{ attenuated | length }} complete window{% if attenuated | length != 1 %}s{% endif %} met this review condition. Sounds present in stereo may be harder to hear in the analyzed copy.</p>{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if evidence.stereo_listening %}
<h4>Compare stereo and analyzed mono</h4>
<p class="caption">Waveforms cover only the {{ evidence.stereo_listening | length }} selected {{ 'interval' if evidence.stereo_listening | length == 1 else 'intervals' }} below. The analysis view provides the matching audio clips. These comparisons carry no weight in the AI assessment.</p>
{% for comparison in evidence.stereo_listening %}
<article class="multimedia-evidence-packet multimedia-repeat-pair">
<h4>Decoded audio {{ '%.3f' | format(comparison.start_s) }}–{{ '%.3f' | format(comparison.end_s) }} s</h4>
<p class="caption">Samples [{{ comparison.start_sample }}, {{ comparison.end_sample }}) at {{ stereo.sample_rate }} Hz.
{% for range in comparison.ranges %}Source PTS [{{ range.source_start_pts }}, {{ range.source_end_pts }}) at {{ range.time_base }}.{% if range.playback %} Video playback {{ '%.3f' | format(range.playback[0]) }}–{{ '%.3f' | format(range.playback[1]) }} s.{% endif %}{% endfor %}
{% if comparison.omitted_ranges %} {{ comparison.omitted_ranges }} additional source-clock ranges in JSON.{% endif %}</p>
{{ plates([comparison.waveform], true) }}
<p class="caption evidence-hash">Waveform SHA-256 <span class="mono">{{ comparison.waveform.sha256 }}</span>.<br>
JSON pointer <span class="mono">{{ comparison.json_pointer }}</span>.</p>
</article>
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
<table class="multimedia-locator">
<thead><tr><th>Decoded range</th><th>Source timestamps (PTS)</th><th>L / R{% if has_downmix %} / mono{% endif %} (dBFS)</th><th>Gap (dB)</th><th>Correlation</th><th>Observation</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>{% for window in stereo.windows %}<tr>
<td>{{ window.start_sample // stereo.sample_rate }}–{{ window.end_sample // stereo.sample_rate }} s</td>
<td>{% for range in window.source_timestamp_ranges %}
{% set start_s = range.source_start_pts / stereo.sample_rate %}
{% set end_s = range.source_end_pts / stereo.sample_rate %}
{{ '%.3f' | format(start_s) }}–{{ '%.3f' | format(end_s) }} s<br>[{{ range.source_start_pts }}, {{ range.source_end_pts }}) at {{ range.time_base }}
{% set video_origin_s = evidence.get('stereo_context_video_origin_s') %}
{% if video_origin_s is not none and start_s >= video_origin_s %}<br>Video playback {{ '%.3f' | format(start_s - video_origin_s) }}–{{ '%.3f' | format(end_s - video_origin_s) }} s{% endif %}
{% if not loop.last %}<br>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</td>
<td>{{ window.left_rms_dbfs }} / {{ window.right_rms_dbfs }}{% if has_downmix %} / {{ window.downmix.mono_rms_dbfs }}{% endif %}</td>
<td>{{ window.level_gap_db if window.level_gap_db is not none else '—' }}</td>
<td>{{ window.correlation if window.correlation is not none else '—' }}</td>
<td>{% if window.status == 'strong_imbalance' %}{{ window.louder_channel | capitalize }} louder{% elif window.status == 'quiet' %}Below review floor{% else %}Measured{% endif %}{% if has_downmix and window.downmix.strong_attenuation %}<br>{% if window.downmix.mono_rms_dbfs == stereo.silence_floor_dbfs %}Mono is digitally silent{% else %}{{ window.downmix.attenuation_db }} dB quieter in mono{% endif %}{% endif %}</td>
</tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
</table>
<p class="caption">A gap of {{ stereo.strong_level_gap_db }} dB or more marks a strong difference for review. {{ stereo.silence_floor_dbfs }} dBFS represents digital silence. Correlation measures similarity between the two signals on a scale of −1 to +1.{% if has_downmix %} A strong mono level drop means the analyzed mono input is at least {{ stereo.strong_downmix_attenuation_db }} dB quieter than the louder stereo channel.{% endif %}</p>
{% endif %}
<p class="caption">JSON pointer <span class="mono">{{ evidence.stereo_context_pointer }}</span>.</p>
</div>
